veloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $A^4$ given that $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/example-4414.json" "file_sha256" "73339b9f7ca1fae3e011a0db0ef2b6d2a69cb2a055600b158333fb6d4a69c9a2" "basis" 1056 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/example-4414.json" "file_sha256" "73339b9f7ca1fae3e011a0db0ef2b6d2a69cb2a055600b158333fb6d4a69c9a2" "basis" 1056 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/example-4417.json" "file_sha256" "f50404291ac1aa09e140bbb16a6e0d012d1f9a5c4d32d34192fbdfa01c59c690" "basis" 1056 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate $D^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & =-{D}^{2}+3D+2I \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3+2 & 10+15+0 \\\\ 0 & -9-9+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/example-4417.json" "file_sha256" "f50404291ac1aa09e140bbb16a6e0d012d1f9a5c4d32d34192fbdfa01c59c690" "basis" 1056 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(D)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "104e1cc63c870b44286075c1b3c2d704c0288450181e6f651aa2c615641e013f" "basis" 1490 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-4I.$ \n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-4I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-4 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & 4-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/state.json" "file_sha256" "104e1cc63c870b44286075c1b3c2d704c0288450181e6f651aa2c615641e013f" "basis" 1490 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041294/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4ae49595829175660b1502c00b26bf0914a802c4abdc6047b3e066dc3a8be17" "basis" 1490 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referenc