| {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to find ${A}^{2},$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${A}^{4}={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}146 & -130 \\\\ 65 & -49\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9923620213817c738d757baf104b046cf604309ccbf8aea300403b45fb514e30"} {"question" "q-279435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answe