value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}-X-2$, find $f(D).$\n\n| $f(D)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-X-2 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-X-2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-D-2I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-D-2I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9-3-2 & -8-(-2)-0 \\\\ 0-0-0 & 1-1-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9923620213817c738d757baf104b046cf604309ccbf8aea300403b45fb514e30"} {"question" "q-279485" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279485" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-279485" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/