 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-2X-8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-2X-8 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-2X-8I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}-2A-8I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 10 \\\\ 15 & 22\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}-2A-8I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 10 \\\\ 15 & 22\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 10 \\\\ 15 & 22\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ -6 & -8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7-2-8 & 10-4+0 \\\\ 15-6+0 & 22-8-8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9923620213817c738d757baf104b046cf604309ccbf8aea300403b45fb51