me/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-4I.$ \n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-4I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-4 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & 4-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9923620213817c738d757baf104b046cf604309ccbf8aea300403b45fb514e30"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "q-130684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/state.json" "file_sha256" "956a4ee55117be96f2b7c9a3adc1946f5bf410ebb8a0e9f110abdb4dcf39f02a"} {"question" "e-4414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $A^4$ given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/assets/45b13bcb5bbd8dc54e605acf6d378f582dcb7a4f2ecfff35a7a5343ee30f0515.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/example-4414.json" "file_sha256" "3a65a0c0061e20c5d15cc590cfe410dac5458b245886a9149b207c283468338c"} {"question" "e-4414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/example-4414.json" "file_sha256" "3a65a0c0061e20c5d15cc590cfe410dac5458b245886a9149b207c283468338c"} {"question" "e-4417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/assets/a58c9caa0812b56d74f38a457c3f39e72a3fd365a881d4128cfd55c1773e05f6.png)\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/example-4417.json" "file_sha256" "c998ca77277f42d452d4cdea26e9fc8c028440cf35e4defd7d0950d56da49177"} {"question" "e-4417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate $D^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & =-{D}^{2}+3D+2I \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3+2 & 10+15+0 \\\\ 0 & -9-9+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/example-4417.json" "file_sha256" "c998ca77277f42d452d4cdea26e9fc8c028440cf35e4defd7d0950d56da49177"}] "usage" {"e-4414" [] "q-78497" [] "q-78529" [] "q-130684" [] "e-4417" []} "basis" 1713 "retractions" [[17592186114976 :question/problem "Find $A^4$ given that $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186114977 :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186284447 17592186284448 17592186284449 17592186284450 17592186284451 17592186284461 17592186284462 17592186284463 17592186284464 17592186284465 17592186310916 17592186310917 17592186310918 17592186310919 17592186310920] "immutable_fields" [[17592186284446 :answer-field/correct] [17592186284446 :answer-field/id] [17592186284446 :answer-field/key] [17592186284446 :answer-field/type] [17592186284460 :answer-field/correct] [17592186284460 :answer-field/id] [17592186284460 :answer-field/key] [17592186284460 :answer-field/type] [17592186310915 :answer-field/correct] [17592186310915 :answer-field/id] [17592186310915 :answer-field/key] [17592186310915 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
